SUMMARY:Deadline: Zindi: Bias Bounty Mapping Equity Challenge
DESCRIPTION:A bias bounty from Zindi\, Humane Intelligence\, Radiant Earth\
 , and the Heising-Simons Foundation: measure coverage gaps in Overture Map
 s across US Census tracts by comparing it against Census TIGER/Line Roads\
 , Microsoft US Building Footprints\, USGS National Map critical facilities
 \, and Census County Business Patterns. Submissions are automatically eval
 uated with a Bias Score assessing equity metrics across demographic and cl
 imate-vulnerability strata\, surfacing whose neighbourhoods open map data 
 underserves. PRIZES: 1st USD 4\,500\, 2nd USD 2\,500\, 3rd USD 1\,500\, Be
 st Bias Discovery USD 1\,000\, Best Documentation USD 500 (USD 10\,000 tot
 al)\, plus 10\,000 Zindi points. ELIGIBILITY: open to all\, teams of up to
  4. HOW TO ENTER: create a Zindi account\, download the sample submission 
 files\, compute coverage-gap scores per tract GEOID\, and upload a CSV\; 1
 0 submissions per day\, 300 total. Free to enter. DEADLINE: 31 October 202
 6.\n\nOrganisation: Zindi with Humane Intelligence\, Radiant Earth\, and t
 he Heising-Simons Foundation\nLocation: Online\, open to all worldwide\; t
 eams of up to 4.\nAward: USD 10\,000 total in prizes: 1st USD 4\,500\, 2nd
  USD 2\,500\, 3rd USD 1\,500\, Best Bias Discovery USD 1\,000\, Best Docum
 entation USD 500\, plus 10\,000 Zindi points. Free to enter.\nDuration: Ru
 ns 28 August to 31 October 2026\; up to 10 submissions per day\, 300 total
 .\n\nMore: https://zindi.world/competitions/bias-bounty-mapping-equity-cha
 llenge?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://zindi.world/competitions/bias-bounty-mapping-equity-challenge?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\, open to all worldwide\; teams of up to 4.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:intron-sahara-codeswitch-africa-challenge-2026@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260921T165832Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Intron: Sahara CodeSwitch Africa Challenge
DESCRIPTION:Intron's Sahara CodeSwitch Africa Challenge awards USD 10\,000 
 in cash prizes for real applications built on African voice AI: apps that 
 understand African-language code-switching\, for example when a speaker mo
 ves between English and Swahili\, English and Igbo\, or French and Wolof m
 id-conversation. TRACKS: Health (clinical documentation\, patient intake\,
  maternal health)\; Legal and Public Services (court transcription\, legal
  aid\, citizen services)\; Fintech\, Telco and Customer Experience (voice 
 banking\, KYC\, payments\, support)\; Agriculture and Education (farmer ad
 visory\, tutoring\, classroom learning)\; and Other High-Impact Use Cases 
 (accessibility\, media\, commerce\, culture). REQUIREMENTS: use voice to a
 chieve a downstream task (not just speech-to-text)\, build with the Intron
  Sahara API\, benchmark Sahara against at least three other speech models\
 , target a specific vertical\, and include code-switched audio samples whe
 re possible. WHO IS ELIGIBLE: developers\, researchers\, startups\, studen
 t teams and NGOs across Africa and the diaspora\; solo or teams. DEADLINE:
  registration and final submissions close 15 September 2026\, 11:59pm WAT\
 , so move fast. Winners announced 1 October 2026. TO APPLY: register at in
 tron.io/compete. Free to enter.\n\nOrganisation: Intron\nLocation: Remote\
 ; open to builders across Africa and the diaspora\, solo or in teams (2 to
  5 recommended).\nAward: USD 10\,000 total prize pool in cash prizes acros
 s five tracks. Finalists also get Sahara API credits\, Partner Demo Day ac
 cess\, visibility with sponsors and judges\, and potential pilot or deploy
 ment conversations. Free to enter.\nDuration: Main competition winners ann
 ounced 1 October 2026\n\nMore: https://intron.io/compete?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://intron.io/compete?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\; open to builders across Africa and the diaspora\, solo or
  in teams (2 to 5 recommended).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mozilla-data-collective-lost-in-transcription-2026@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20260921T165832Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261003
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mozilla Data Collective: Lost in Transcription ASR Challe
 nge
DESCRIPTION:Lost in Transcription: Advancing Speech Recognition for Underse
 rved Linguistic Contexts is a machine learning competition on the Mozilla 
 Data Collective platform (run with DrivenData\, backed by Mozilla Foundati
 on). Participants build automatic speech recognition (ASR) models for real
 -world bilingual\, code-switched conversations across three independent tr
 acks: Nahuatl x Spanish\, Indonesian x Javanese\, and North American Spani
 sh x English (Spanglish)\; developers can also work with other languages i
 f the datasets are available on or uploaded to the MDC platform\, which of
 fers ethically sourced multilingual\, multicultural and multimodal dataset
 s. PRIZES: USD 20\,000 total\; per track USD 4\,000 for first place and US
 D 2\,000 for second\, judged by word error rate on a private leaderboard\,
  plus a bonus award for the lowest average word error rate across all thre
 e tracks (same team members required). WHO IS ELIGIBLE: individuals and te
 ams worldwide (students\, tech clubs\, universities\, startup builders\, l
 abs\, independent tinkerers)\; 18+ and legal resident of an eligible juris
 diction\; one account per person\; participants are responsible for comply
 ing with school or employer policies. DEADLINE: the platform lists final s
 ubmissions closing 2 October 2026\, midnight UTC (some announcements said 
 25 September\, so check the platform for your track). Free to enter.\n\nOr
 ganisation: Mozilla Data Collective (Mozilla Foundation)\nLocation: Online
 \, worldwide. Participants must be 18+ (and of age of majority in their ju
 risdiction) and legal residents of an eligible territory\; residents of so
 me territories are excluded from prizes.\nAward: USD 20\,000 total in priz
 es across three language tracks (per track: USD 4\,000 for first place and
  USD 2\,000 for second\, plus a bonus award for the lowest average word er
 ror rate across all three tracks). No entry fee.\nDuration: Winners determ
 ined by word error rate on a private leaderboard after the 2 October 2026 
 close\n\nMore: https://competitions.mozilladatacollective.com/competitions
 /1/lost-in-transcription/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://competitions.mozilladatacollective.com/competitions/1/lost-in-t
 ranscription/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\, worldwide. Participants must be 18+ (and of age of majori
 ty in their jurisdiction) and legal residents of an eligible territory\; r
 esidents of some territories are excluded from prizes.
END:VEVENT
